      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to determine the dimensions of the rectangle using the information given about walking distance.\n\n1. **Investigate how Mateen traversed his backyard using lengths and perimeters:**\n\n   - Mateen walked the length 25 times to cover 1 kilometer.\n   - Mateen walked the perimeter 10 times to cover 1 kilometer.\n\n2. **Determine the total paths for measurement:**\n\n   - The perimeter \\( P \\) is:\n     \\[\n     P = 10 \\text{ kilometers}\n     \\]\n     Since 1 kilometer is equal to 1000 meters, the perimeter in meters is:\n     \\[\n     P = 10 \\times 1000 = 10000 \\text{ meters}\n     \\]\n     \n   - The length \\( L \\) walked 25 times to cover 1 kilometer:\n     \\[\n     L = 25 \\text{ times}\n     \\]\n     Therefore, the length of the backyard in meters is:\n     \\[\n     L = \\frac{10000 \\text{ meters}}{25} = 400 \\text{ meters}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Relate the perimeter and length to the area:**\n\n   - Let the width of the backyard be \\( W \\).\n   - The perimeter of the rectangle, using the length \\( L \\) and width \\( W \\), is given by:\n     \\[\n     P = 2L + 2W\n     \\]\n     Substituting \\( P = 10000 \\text{ meters} \\) and \\( L = 400 \\text{ meters} \\):\n     \\[\n     10000 = 2 \\times 400 + 2W\n     \\]\n     Simplify to solve for \\( W \\):\n     \\[\n     10000 = 800 + 2W\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     9200 = 2W\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     W = \\frac{9200}{2} = 4600 \\text{ meters}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the area of the backyard:**\n\n   - The area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n     \\[\n     A = L \\times W\n     \\]\n     Substituting \\( L = 400 \\text{ meters} \\) and \\( W = 4600 \\text{ meters} \\):\n     \\[\n     A = 400 \\times 4600 = 1840000 \\text{ square meters}\n     \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{1840000}\\).",
