      "text": "Let \"l\" be the length of Mateen's backyard and \"w\" be the width. The perimeter is 2l + 2w, so we can write the following equation: \n\n25l = 2l + 2w = 10 times (2l + 2w)\n\n25l = 20l + 20w\n5l = 20w\nl = 4 w\nl = 2 w\n\nSo the backyard has the following properties:\n\nl =2 w\nl +w = 1000 m\n2w + w = 1000 m\n3w = 1000 m\nw = 333.33 m\n\nNow we can substitute one of the unknowns back into either equation to get the already determined value:\n\nl = 2 w\nl = 2(333.33 m)\nl = 666.66 m\n\nThe area is therefore:\n\nA = l × w\nA = 666.66 m × 333.33 m\nA = 216666 m^2.\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is 216666 square meters.",
